        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Spectral and Random Graph Methods",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The graph Laplacian **L = D − A** (degree matrix minus adjacency) is the single\nmost important matrix in spectral graph theory. Its eigenvalues encode global\nconnectivity structure that no local computation reveals."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-SPECTRAL-AND-RANDOM.md#011",
      "path": [
        "08-SPECTRAL-AND-RANDOM.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:graph-algorithms:08-spectral-and-random, git-history:graph-algorithms:08-spectral-and-random]",
        "canonical_path": "graph-algorithms/08-SPECTRAL-AND-RANDOM.md",
        "concepts": "[Laplacian, spectral clustering, PageRank, random walks, expanders, eigenvalues]",
        "current_path": "graph-algorithms/08-SPECTRAL-AND-RANDOM.md",
        "id": "maxim:graph-algorithms:spectral-and-random",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "graph-algorithms",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[spectral graph theory]",
        "section": "mathematics-physics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Spectral and Random Graph Methods",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  Key facts about L = D - A (undirected graph):\n  ---------------------------------------------\n  * L is symmetric, positive SEMI-definite: all eigenvalues lambda_i >= 0.\n  * lambda_1 = 0 ALWAYS (the all-ones vector 1 is in the kernel: L*1 = 0).\n  * MULTIPLICITY of eigenvalue 0 = number of connected components.\n      (a path graph: mult 1; two disjoint triangles: mult 2.)\n  * lambda_2 > 0  <=>  the graph is connected.  lambda_2 is the FIEDLER VALUE\n      / algebraic connectivity -- bigger means \"harder to disconnect\"."
    }
